# pipenv
#   According to pypa.io/pipenv/usage.html#installing-your-program-using-pipenv
#   Pipfile.lock is expected to be checked into version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies
#   or dependency versions which are not cross-platform compatible,
#   Pipfile.lock may not be checked in.
#   If you want to override this, uncomment the line below.
# Pipfile.lock

# Pypoetry
#   According to pypoetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-pycrojecttoml-to-version-control
#   pyproject.toml and poetry.lock are expected to be checked into version control.
#   However, if there are platform-specific dependencies or
#   dependency versions which are not cross-platform compatible,
#   poetry.lock may not be checked in.
#   If you want to override this, uncomment the line below.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   According to pdm-farm.github.io/pdm/usage/installing-your-program/#dependencies
#   pdm.lock is expected to be checked into version control.
#   However, if there are platform-specific dependencies or
#   dependency versions which are not cross-platform compatible,
#   pdm.lock may not be checked in.
#   If you want to override this, uncomment the line below.
# pdm.lock

